  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nThere are $n$ urns each containing $(n+1)$ balls such that the ith urn contains $i$ white balls and $(n+1-i)$ red balls. Let $u_i$ be the event of selecting ith urn, $i=1,2,3, \\ldots, n$ and $W$ denotes the event of getting a white balls.<strong>Question:</strong>\nIf $n$ is even and $E$ denotes the event of choosing even numbered urn $\\left(P\\left(u_i\\right)=\\frac{1}{n}\\right)$, then the value of $P(W / E)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Nu9pl",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n+2}{2 n+1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yA5ZB",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n+2}{2(n+1)}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tqFsT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n}{n+1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nwyVw",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{n+1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$P(W / E)=\\frac{2+4+6+\\ldots}{\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}}=\\frac{n+2}{2(n+1)}$",
    "image": null
  },
